          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="465f-42b7-9af3-fc0e" type="set" value="1">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="0176-56a3-d590-b103" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="63f0-9b87-6482-87ee" shared="true" type="greaterThan" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="0176-56a3-d590-b103" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="63f0-9b87-6482-87ee" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Warlord Trait: The End and the Death" id="8a1c-2701-a509-cf26" hidden="false" page="21" publicationId="8775-88f5-cfdd-24f6" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">Samus Unbound may always be selected as an army’s Warlord even if it is not part of the Primary Detachment or a HQ choice. If chosen as the army’s  Warlord, Samus Unbound replaces the Empyrean Avatar special rule with the Eternal Warrior  special rule and automatically has The End and the Death as its Warlord Trait and may not select any other.

The End and the Death – When fighting in a Challenge, successful Invulnerable Saves taken against Samus Unbound’s attacks must be re-rolled. In addition, an army with Samus Unbound as its Warlord may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player&apos;s Movement phase as long as Samus Unbound has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry name="Ætheric Conduit" id="9c2-edf8-c9bd-ec05" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <constraints>
